libnginx-mod-http-coraza (0.21.0-0keel1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First Keel package (handbook decision 0041, first implementation,
    step 5): Coraza's Nginx connector as a dynamic module of trixie's
    nginx 1.26.3. Not in Debian and no ITP. dh-sequence-nginx builds it
    against nginx-dev and makes it depend on nginx-abi-1.26.3-1, as
    trixie's own libnginx-mod-* packages do, so it is rebuilt whenever
    trixie's nginx moves to another upstream version.
  * The module loads libcoraza with dlopen in each worker, so the
    dependency on libcoraza1 is declared rather than computed;
    soname-dlopen.patch, from upstream's own Debian packaging, loads the
    versioned libcoraza.so.1.
  * debian/tests: with the OWASP Core Rule Set of the coreruleset
    package, a normal request gets 200 and SQL injection and
    cross-site scripting payloads get 403.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
